<title>FINLAND: FINVEST ALSO TO SELL INTERGLOBIA STAKE.</title>
<headline>FINVEST ALSO TO SELL INTERGLOBIA STAKE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish capacitor and consulting group Finvest said in a statement on Tuesday it had approved Canadian Beninco Holdings' bid for its 51.2 percent stake in real estate investment company InterGlobia.</p>
<p>In connection with the deal, Finvest would buy two buildings and one piece of land from Interglobia.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal will have no significant impact on Finvest group's result in 1997,&quot; Finvest said.</p>
<p>Interavanti said earlier Beninco had offered to buy all of InterGlobia and that it had approved the offer for its 25.2 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
